{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Sales Analytics & Demand Forecasting for Dairy Products\n","\n","**Tools:** Python, SQL, Power BI, Microsoft Excel, Pandas, Scikit-learn\n","\n","## Business objective\n","Analyse a large-scale dairy sales dataset to identify sales trends, inventory patterns and pricing strategies, then compare four predictive models—Linear Regression, Decision Tree, SVM and Neural Network—for demand forecasting.\n","\n","**Important:** All KPI and model results below are calculated from the supplied 50,000-row dataset when the notebook is run; no results are hard-coded."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import pandas as pd\n","import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n","from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n","from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder, StandardScaler\n","from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n","from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n","from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeRegressor\n","from sklearn.svm import SVR\n","from sklearn.neural_network import MLPRegressor\n","from sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error, mean_squared_error, r2_score\n","\n","df = pd.read_csv('../data/dairy_sales_50000.csv', parse_dates=['Date'])\n","df.shape, df.head()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Data quality, cleaning and preprocessing"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["print(\"Missing values:\\n\", df.isna().sum())\n","print(\"Duplicate rows:\", df.duplicated().sum())\n","\n","df = df.drop_duplicates().copy()\n","df['Revenue'] = df['Unit_Price'] * df['Units_Sold'] * (1 - df['Discount_Pct']/100)\n","df['Profit'] = df['Revenue'] * 0.25\n","df['Year'] = df['Date'].dt.year\n","df['Month'] = df['Date'].dt.month\n","df['DayOfWeek'] = df['Date'].dt.dayofweek\n","\n","print(\"Cleaned shape:\", df.shape)\n","display(df.describe(include='all').T)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Exploratory Data Analysis"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["monthly = df.groupby(df['Date'].dt.to_period('M')).agg(\n","    Revenue=('Revenue','sum'), Units_Sold=('Units_Sold','sum'), Profit=('Profit','sum')\n",").reset_index()\n","monthly['Date'] = monthly['Date'].dt.to_timestamp()\n","\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12,5))\n","ax.plot(monthly['Date'], monthly['Revenue'])\n","ax.set_title('Monthly Revenue Trend')\n","ax.set_xlabel('Month'); ax.set_ylabel('Revenue')\n","plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n","\n","product_summary = df.groupby(['Product','Category']).agg(\n","    Units_Sold=('Units_Sold','sum'), Revenue=('Revenue','sum'), Profit=('Profit','sum')\n",").sort_values('Revenue', ascending=False)\n","display(product_summary.head(10))\n","\n","region_summary = df.groupby('Region')[['Revenue','Profit','Units_Sold']].sum().sort_values('Revenue', ascending=False)\n","display(region_summary)\n","\n","channel_summary = df.groupby('Channel')[['Revenue','Profit','Units_Sold']].sum().sort_values('Revenue', ascending=False)\n","display(channel_summary)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Pricing and inventory analysis"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["discount_summary = df.groupby(\n","    pd.cut(df['Discount_Pct'], bins=[-1,4,9,14,100],\n","           labels=['0–4%','5–9%','10–14%','15%+'])\n")[['Units_Sold','Revenue','Profit']].sum()\n","display(discount_summary)\n","\n","inventory = df.groupby(['Product','Category']).agg(\n","    Avg_Demand=('Units_Sold','mean'), Total_Units=('Units_Sold','sum'),\n","    Revenue=('Revenue','sum'), Profit=('Profit','sum')\n").sort_values('Avg_Demand', ascending=False)\n","display(inventory.head(10))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. Demand forecasting — four models"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["features = ['Year','Month','DayOfWeek','Product','Category','Region',\n","            'Channel','Customer_Type','Unit_Price','Discount_Pct']\n","X = df[features]\n","y = df['Units_Sold']\n","\n","cat_cols = ['Product','Category','Region','Channel','Customer_Type']\n","num_cols = ['Year','Month','DayOfWeek','Unit_Price','Discount_Pct']\n","\n","preprocess = ColumnTransformer([\n","    ('cat', OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore'), cat_cols),\n","    ('num', StandardScaler(), num_cols)\n,"])\n","\n","X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n","    X, y, test_size=0.20, random_state=42\n,")\n","\n","models = {\n","    'Linear Regression': LinearRegression(),\n","    'Decision Tree': DecisionTreeRegressor(max_depth=12, random_state=42),\n","    # SVM is trained on a representative sample because kernel SVR is computationally expensive on 50,000 rows.\n","    'SVM': SVR(C=10, epsilon=0.1),\n","    'Neural Network': MLPRegressor(hidden_layer_sizes=(64,32), max_iter=300,\n","                                   random_state=42, early_stopping=True)\n,}\n","\n","results = []\n","for name, estimator in models.items():\n","    X_fit, y_fit = X_train, y_train\n","    if name == 'SVM' and len(X_fit) > 10000:\n","        sample_idx = X_fit.sample(10000, random_state=42).index\n","        X_fit, y_fit = X_fit.loc[sample_idx], y_fit.loc[sample_idx]\n","    pipe = Pipeline([('preprocess', preprocess), ('model', estimator)])\n","    pipe.fit(X_fit, y_fit)\n","    pred = pipe.predict(X_test)\n","    results.append({\n","        'Model': name,\n","        'MAE': mean_absolute_error(y_test, pred),\n","        'RMSE': mean_squared_error(y_test, pred) ** 0.5,\n","        'R2': r2_score(y_test, pred)\n","    })\n","\n","results_df = pd.DataFrame(results).sort_values('RMSE')\n","display(results_df)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. Output and findings\n","\n","The next cell generates the project’s final KPI summary and automatically selects the best model by RMSE. This makes the findings reproducible rather than manually entered."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["kpis = {\n","    'Transactions': len(df),\n","    'Total Revenue': df['Revenue'].sum(),\n","    'Total Profit': df['Profit'].sum(),\n","    'Units Sold': df['Units_Sold'].sum(),\n","    'Top Region': region_summary.index[0],\n","    'Top Product': product_summary.index[0][0],\n","    'Best Forecasting Model': results_df.iloc[0]['Model']\n,}\n","display(pd.Series(kpis, name='Value'))\n","\n","print('Conclusion:')\n","print(f\"The analysis covers {kpis['Transactions']:,} transactions. {kpis['Top Region']} is the highest-revenue region and {kpis['Top Product']} is the highest-revenue product. The best model by RMSE in this run is {kpis['Best Forecasting Model']}. Use these outputs with the Power BI dashboard for inventory and pricing decisions.\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 6. Power BI dashboard\n","\n","Import `data/powerbi_ready_sales.csv` into Power BI and build:\n","- KPI cards: Revenue, Profit, Units Sold, Orders\n","- Monthly Revenue Trend\n","- Regional Performance\n","- Product Performance\n","- Sales Channel Performance\n","- Slicers: Date, Region, Product, Channel, Customer Type\n","\n","Dashboard screenshots are stored in `images/`."]}],"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.x"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5}